      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we first need to understand the number of days between November 23 and December 23.\n\n1. **Determine the Number of Days:**\n   - From November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n   - From December 1 to December 23 is \\(23 - 1 = 22\\) days.\n   - So, the total number of days from November 23 to December 23 is \\(8 + 22 = 30\\) days.\n\n2. **Calculate Weeks and Days:**\n   - Since there are 7 days in a week, we divide 30 days by 7 to find the number of complete weeks and the remaining days.\n   - \\(30 \\div 7 = 4\\) weeks and \\(2\\) days with a remainder of \\(2\\) days.\n   - This means that 30 days is equivalent to 4 weeks and 2 additional days.\n\n3. **Determine the Day of the Week:**\n   - If November 23 was a Thursday, then adding 2 days will give us the day of the week for December 23.\n   - November 23 is a Thursday.\n   - Adding 2 days to Thursday gives us Saturday.\n\nThus, December 23 is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).",
