      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving falls on Thursday, November 23. We can do this by calculating the number of days from November 23 to December 23 and then finding the corresponding day of the week.\n\nThe number of days between November 23 and December 23 is:\n\\[ 23 - 23 + 30 = 30 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nThis is because we count from November 23 to December 23, which is 30 days.\n\nNext, we need to determine what day of the week it is 30 days after Thursday. We can do this by finding the remainder when 30 is divided by 7 (since there are 7 days in a week):\n\\[ 30 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ R } 2 \\]\nThis means that 30 days is equivalent to 4 weeks and 2 additional days. Starting from Thursday, adding 2 days gives us:\n\\[ \\text{Thursday} + 2 \\text{ days} = \\text{Saturday} \\]\n\nTherefore, December 23 occurs on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).",
